{
  "id": "qudud_halabiyya",
  "name": "Al-Qudūd al-Ḥalabiyya (Aleppine measured song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Repertoire of measured songs associated with Aleppo, many setting secular words to older religious melodies, sung in maqam by a soloist and chorus with a takht of oud, qanun, nay, violin and riq, and performed in suites alongside muwashshahat at weddings, gatherings and concerts. It is on the UNESCO Representative List and was carried to wide audiences on radio, records and the concert stage from the 1950s onward by singers such as Sabah Fakhri and Sabri Moudallal.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1950s al-qudūd al-ḥalabiyya, art Music, middle eastern classical branch. multi note runs per syllable, neutral third half flat, arab mawwal layali maqam modulation. oud, articulate metal finger picks qanun, credited ney, fiddle, brass jingles canonical takht riq. live tracking. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
  "recipe_chars": 401,
